In `files/testcase.py`, the `Faker("en_GB")` instance is seeded, then `city()` and `street_name()` are called before `postcode()`, so those earlier provider calls advance the same instance RNG before `postcode()` selects a template. In `faker/providers/address/en_GB/__init__.py`, `postcode()` stores `pattern = self.random_element(self.postcode_formats)` before expanding each placeholder through `_postcode_sets`. For this seeded call sequence, the selected template is `"PND NEE"`.

## Answer
{"postcode_pattern":"PND NEE"}
